        "answer": "Hexagram 5 — Waiting (Xu) is the fifth hexagram of the I Ching. The upper trigram is Kan (Water/Clouds) and the lower trigram is Qian (Heaven). Clouds gather above the sky, building up yet not yet releasing rain — this is the image of 'Water Heaven Xu.' The character 'Xu' means to wait or to need. The hexagram centers on the theme of waiting wisely: when danger (Kan) lies ahead and the time is not yet ripe, even with the strength of Heaven (Qian), one must learn to wait. This is not weakness, but wisdom."
