    "guaCiZh": "謙：亨，君子有終。",
    "imageCommentaryEn": "Within the earth, a mountain: the image of Modesty. Thus the superior person reduces that which is too much, and augments that which is too little. He weighs things and makes them equal.",
    "imageCommentaryZh": "地中有山，謙。君子以裒多益寡，稱物平施。",
    "overviewEn": "Modesty (Qian) is the fifteenth hexagram. The lower trigram is Gen (Mountain) and the upper is Kun (Earth). A mountain hidden beneath the earth — immense power and substance completely concealed beneath a surface of humility. This is the most universally praised hexagram in the I Ching: the only one where every single line is favorable.\nThe judgment is simple and profound: 'Modesty creates success.' This is not mere politeness but a cosmic principle — heaven diminishes the proud and augments the humble; earth overthrows the full and fills the modest. The Image teaches practical balance: 'reduce what is too much, augment what is too little.' True modesty is not self-deprecation but accurate self-assessment combined with generous redistribution. The mountain beneath the earth has nothing to prove — its substance is undeniable regardless of its visible height.",
    "overviewZh": "謙（qiān）卦，是易經六十四卦之第十五卦。從卦象上看，上卦為坤（地），下卦為艮（山）。山原本高聳入雲，此刻卻靜靜地沉潛在大地的懷抱之中。這種高山仰止卻甘願處下的姿態，正是謙卦的核心精神。在萬物競相爭高、急功近利的社會中，謙卦獨樹一幟地指出了退後、守卑、虛懷若谷的巨大力量。\n卦辭極其簡練：“亨，君子有終”。這意味著謙遜不僅能帶來當前的亨通，更能讓你在漫長的人生馬拉松中笑到最後。大象傳提到的“裒多益寡，稱物平施”，則是提醒我們要像大地一樣，調節盈餘與不足，追求一種動態的平衡與公正。這是一個關於修身、齊家、治企的頂級智慧卦象。",
