    "imageCommentaryEn": "Thunder comes resounding out of the earth: the image of Enthusiasm. Thus the ancient kings made music in order to honor merit, and offered it with splendor to the Supreme Deity, inviting their ancestors to be present.",
    "imageCommentaryZh": "雷出地奮，豫。先王以作樂崇德，殷薦之上帝，以配祖考。",
    "overviewEn": "Enthusiasm (Yu) is the sixteenth hexagram. The lower trigram is Kun (Earth) and the upper is Zhen (Thunder). Thunder bursting from the earth — a sudden, dramatic release of energy that stirs everything to life. This is the image of Enthusiasm: a joyful, irresistible force that moves people to willing action.\nThe judgment says it 'furthers one to install helpers and to set armies marching' — Enthusiasm is the energy that mobilizes. When people are genuinely inspired, they move willingly and powerfully. The ancient kings understood this: they made music not just for entertainment but to unite the people's hearts and inspire collective action. In modern terms, Enthusiasm is about leadership that inspires rather than compels, energy that comes from genuine joy rather than forced effort.",
    "overviewZh": "豫（yù）卦，是易經六十四卦之第十六卦。從卦象上看，上卦為震（雷），下卦為坤（地）。春雷在大地上炸響，驚醒了冬眠的萬物，大地感應到震動的力量而奮發向上，這是一幅充滿生機、歡欣鼓舞的圖景。豫卦的核心內涵在於喜悅與順應，它告訴我們，當人心歡愉、順勢而動時，沒有什麼困難是不能克服的。\n卦辭“利建侯行師”，意味著此時正是確立大計、調兵遣將、大刀闊斧開展事業的良機。大象傳提到先王透過創作音樂來崇尚美德、祭祀祖先，這揭示了豫卦與文化、藝術、儀式感的深刻聯絡。在這個階段，情緒價值和精神凝聚力往往比硬性的物質激勵更具威力。這是一個關於如何動員群體力量、在歡樂中成就偉業的卦象。",
