    "guaCiEn": "Contemplation. The ablution has been made, but not yet the offering. Full of trust they look up to him.",
    "guaCiZh": "觀：盥而不薦，有孚顒若。",
    "imageCommentaryEn": "The wind blows over the earth: the image of Contemplation. Thus the kings of old visited the regions of the world, contemplated the people, and gave them instruction.",
    "imageCommentaryZh": "風行地上，觀。先王以省方觀民設教。",
    "overviewEn": "Contemplation (Guan) is the twentieth hexagram. The lower trigram is Kun (Earth) and the upper is Xun (Wind). Wind blowing over the earth reaches everywhere, seeing everything — the image of comprehensive observation and deep contemplation.\nThe judgment describes a sacred moment: 'The ablution has been made, but not yet the offering.' The priest has purified himself but has not yet begun the ceremony. This is the moment of pure, focused attention — the quality of mind that sees deeply into the nature of things. Contemplation works in two directions: you observe the world, and the world observes you. The quality of your inner life determines what you see and what others see in you.",
    "overviewZh": "觀卦是易經六十四卦之第二十卦。從卦象上看，上卦為巽代表風，下卦為坤代表地。風在大地上吹拂，無孔不入，象徵著廣泛的周遊與深入的考察。觀的雙重含義是“觀看”與“展示”。當你站得高時，你是觀察者；當你被眾人矚目時，你是被觀者。大象傳提到省方觀民設教，揭示了管理者透過考察民情來設立教化的智慧。這一卦的核心精髓在於洞察力與感召力的統一，提醒我們要用客觀的眼光審視環境，用深刻的內省完善自我。",
