    "cardTitleZh": "易羅解讀",
    "guaCiEn": "Return. Success. Going out and coming in without error. Friends come without blame. To and fro goes the way. On the seventh day comes return. It furthers one to have somewhere to go.",
    "guaCiZh": "復：亨。出入無疾，朋來無咎。反覆其道，七日來複。利有攸往。",
    "imageCommentaryEn": "Thunder within the earth: the image of the Turning Point. Thus the kings of antiquity closed the passes at the time of the solstice. Merchants and travelers did not go about, and the ruler did not travel through the provinces.",
    "imageCommentaryZh": "雷在地中，復。先王以至日閉關，商旅不行，後不省方。",
    "overviewEn": "Return (Fu) is the twenty-fourth hexagram — and one of the most hopeful in the entire I Ching. The lower trigram is Zhen (Thunder) and the upper is Kun (Earth). A single yang line appears at the bottom beneath five yin lines: the first spark of light returning after the darkness of Splitting Apart.\nThunder stirring deep within the earth — the winter solstice moment when, though cold still reigns, the cycle has turned and light begins to grow again. The judgment promises success: 'going out and coming in without error, friends come without blame.' The natural order is being restored. The Image counsels rest during this transition: the ancient kings 'closed the passes at the solstice' — understanding that the turning point requires stillness and protection, not premature action.",
    "overviewZh": "復（fù）卦是易經六十四卦之第二十四卦。從卦象上看，上卦為坤代表地，下卦為震代表雷。雷聲在地底震動，象徵著嚴冬中那一絲最寶貴的陽氣正在萌動。大象傳提到先王以至日閉關，暗示在轉機初現的時刻，應當保持安靜，收斂能量，不要急於奔波。復卦代表了迴圈的節律——無論剝落得多麼徹底，只要核心生機不滅，就一定能迎來回歸。這不僅是季節的更替，更是心靈的重啟和秩序的重建。它提醒我們，耐心守候那一縷初生的光芒，整個世界都將隨之復甦。",
