        "divinationEn": {
          "Career": "The top line warns against impulsively quitting or making drastic career changes simply because you're bored with your stable job. 'Restlessness in duration brings misfortune' — directionless change is more dangerous than no change at all. If you genuinely feel your current work no longer fulfills you, create a planned transition rather than flipping the table in a moment of frustration. You can explore new possibilities while keeping your current position — gradual change is far safer than sudden upheaval.",
          "Relationships": "In love, Six at the Top is a stark warning against the 'seven-year itch' crisis in long-term relationships. Stable relationships can breed 'this is all there is' ennui — then one day an inappropriate person appears or an inappropriate thought arises and you start doing reckless things. 'Misfortune' — such impulses will destroy the relationship you built with years of devotion. If you feel the relationship needs fresh air — seek it together with your partner (travel, new hobbies, deep conversations), not behind their back.",
          "Wealth": "Financially, the top line warns against abandoning a long-term steady-income strategy for an impulsive all-in gamble out of boredom. 'Restlessness in duration brings misfortune' — the person who steadily earns 8% annually ends up far wealthier than those who bet everything, double up, then go to zero. If you find investing boring — that means you're doing it right. Boring investments are often the most profitable.",
          "Health": "For health, the top line warns against suddenly indulging after maintaining a healthy lifestyle for a long time — 'my body is so strong, one binge can't hurt.' Years of accumulated health capital can be severely depleted by one extreme indulgence. Also watch your mental health — a state that's outwardly calm but internally high-pressure may suddenly collapse one day. Find outlets for stress release — exercise, talking, vacations — don't let the internal 'magma' build to an uncontrollable level."
        },
        "divinationZh": {
          "事業運勢": "上六爻在事業方面警告你不要因為厭倦了當前的穩定工作就衝動裸辭或做出激進的職業轉變。「振恆，兇」——沒有方向的改變比不變更危險。如果你確實覺得當前的工作已經不能滿足你——制定一個有計劃的轉型方案，而不是一時衝動掀翻桌子。可以在保住現有工作的同時探索新的可能性——漸變比突變安全得多。",
          "感情運勢": "感情方面，上六爻是對長期關係中「七年之癢」式危機的嚴厲警告。穩定的關係會讓人產生「日子就這樣了」的倦怠感——然後某天一個不該出現的人出現了、一個不該有的想法冒出來了——你開始做一些「振恆」的蠢事。「兇」——這種衝動會摧毀你用多年心血建立的關係。如果你覺得感情需要新鮮感——和伴侶一起尋找（旅行、新愛好、深度對話），而不是揹著伴侶去外面找。",
          "財運分析": "財運方面，上六爻警告你不要因為長期的小額穩定收益而不耐煩——然後把所有錢砸進一個高風險的投機專案。「振恆，兇」——每年穩定賺8%的人最終比那些賭一把翻倍然後歸零的人富得多。如果你覺得投資太無聊——那說明你做對了。無聊的投資往往是最賺錢的。",
          "健康提示": "健康方面，上六爻提醒你不要在長期健康的生活方式中突然放縱——「反正我身體這麼好，偶爾放縱一下沒事」。長期積累的健康資本可能在一次極端的放縱中嚴重受損。同時也關注心理健康——長期高壓但表面平靜的狀態可能在某天突然崩潰。找到釋放壓力的出口——運動、傾訴、休假——不要讓內部的「岩漿」積累到不可控的程度。"
        },
