        "yaoTextEn": "Six in the Fifth: Loses the ram at the boundary. No remorse.",
        "yaoTextZh": "六五：喪羊於易，無悔",
        "summaryEn": "Losing the stubborn ram in the open field brings no regret. When you release your aggressive, headstrong energy, you actually gain freedom. The ram symbolized forceful will; losing it means letting go of the need to force outcomes. With this release comes peace and proper alignment.",
        "summaryZh": "六五：喪羊於易，無悔。大壯卦六五爻——羊散在田野中卻無悔恨，以柔馭剛的最高智慧。",
        "tuanEn": "The Tuan Commentary says: The Power of the Great — the great is powerful. The firm moves and is dynamic — hence The Power of the Great. 'The Power of the Great: Perseverance furthers' — the great one is in the correct position. The great correctness reveals the nature of heaven and earth.",
        "tuanZh": "彖曰：大壯，大者壯也。剛以動，故壯。大壯利貞，大者正也。正大而天地之情可見矣。",
